## Original Content
Most evacuees have been allowed to return to their homes near burn zones in Spokane, despite concerns about lingering toxins.

## Summary
Most evacuees in Spokane have been allowed to return home near wildfire burn zones, but the area remains a hazmat situation due to lingering toxins. Authorities have permitted the return despite ongoing health and safety concerns.

## Key Points
- Evacuees are returning to their homes near wildfire burn zones in Spokane.
- Lingering toxins from wildfires pose potential health risks.
- The situation is still classified as a hazardous materials (hazmat) scenario.
- Authorities have allowed the return despite the presence of toxins.


